# Layout and space

## Depth

- Depth is **weight and scale first**, not shadow. A heavier weight, a larger size, a warmer hue — these create hierarchy better than drop shadows.
- When a surface genuinely needs shadow, [`depth.md`](depth.md) owns the system: pick ONE depth language (flat / elevated / glass) and, in the elevated language, use the layered 3-tier shadow scale defined there (a real shadow = subtle ambient + directional layer). For flat-language pages, the closest thing to shadow is the **hairline** — `0 0 0 1px oklch(30% 0.01 <hue> / 0.06)` as an alternative to a 1px border.
- Never use a coloured glow on a light background, and never drop-shadow a dark card (it reads as glow).
- Z-index has **seven levels, named.** Don't freestyle numbers.

```css
:root {
  --z-base:     1;
  --z-raised:   10;
  --z-dropdown: 100;
  --z-sticky:   200;
  --z-modal:    400;
  --z-toast:    500;
  --z-tooltip:  600;
}
```
